            <div class="lesson-body">
                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>.NET Health Checks</h2>
                    <p>Example shows registering health checks for database and broker and mapping separate endpoints for liveness and readiness probes.</p>
                    <pre><code class="language-csharp">// Program.cs
builder.Services.AddHealthChecks()
    .AddSqlServer(connectionString, name: "database")
    .AddRabbitMQ(rabbitMqConnection, name: "rabbitmq")
    .AddCheck("self", () =&gt; HealthCheckResult.Healthy());

app.MapHealthChecks("/health/live", new HealthCheckOptions
{
    Predicate = check =&gt; check.Name == "self"
});

app.MapHealthChecks("/health/ready", new HealthCheckOptions
{
    Predicate = _ =&gt; true
});</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Kubernetes Probes</h2>
                    <p>YAML example demonstrating how to wire Kubernetes liveness, readiness, and startup probes to the app's health endpoints.</p>
                    <pre><code class="language-yaml">spec:
  containers:
  - name: order-service
    livenessProbe:
      httpGet:
        path: /health/live
        port: 80
      initialDelaySeconds: 10
      periodSeconds: 10
    readinessProbe:
      httpGet:
        path: /health/ready
        port: 80
      initialDelaySeconds: 5
      periodSeconds: 5
    startupProbe:
      httpGet:
        path: /health/live
        port: 80
      failureThreshold: 30
      periodSeconds: 10</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Probe Types</h2>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Liveness:</strong> Is the app running? Restart if fails.</li>
                        <li><strong>Readiness:</strong> Can the app handle traffic? Remove from load balancer if fails.</li>
                        <li><strong>Startup:</strong> Has the app finished starting? Runs before liveness/readiness.</li>
                    </ul>
                </section>

                <LessonTakeaways>
                    <LessonTakeaway>Liveness checks if app is alive (restart if not).</LessonTakeaway>
                    <LessonTakeaway>Readiness checks if app can handle traffic.</LessonTakeaway>
                    <LessonTakeaway>Use .NET health checks library.</LessonTakeaway>
                </LessonTakeaways>
            </div>
